1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Branch operations and incident recovery for fast-food and takeaway chains.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Branch A has ingredients, but equipment faults block its menu.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Define the need: five beef-rice servings for Branch A within 60 minutes.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
A support branch must pass menu, stock, equipment and delivery-route checks.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Approve a directed route from Branch B to A: 10 minutes, ¥600.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Select the ingredients stocked at Branch B. Quantities belong to each branch.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Receive stock with a reason. The new balance and movement history are recorded.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:18,640
Register a working fryer for Branch B, with an explicit owning branch.

9
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:28,640
Choose which dishes Branch B offers and set its operating hours.

10
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:37,840
An additional working fryer makes Branch A's menu available. Incident history remains.

11
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:42,040
Track operating status separately from incident history.

12
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:54,440
Request AI advice for manager review. Operational changes still need confirmation.

13
00:01:54,440 --> 00:02:00,920
Branch B is still blocked: a missing griller and a dish travel limit.

14
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:10,120
Add a working griller to Branch B. Equipment requirements are checked per dish.

15
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:21,880
Record a fryer fault at Branch B and request four fried-chicken servings.

16
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:28,880
Approve the return direction separately: Branch A to Branch B.

17
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:38,360
Transfer blocked: 10 minutes of travel exceeds the dish's 3-minute limit.

18
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:46,840
No eligible source means no transfer is created. Managers must review the constraints.
